    "name": "Lecture 1 - Authentication",
    "description": "# E-commerce Training API — Lecture 1: Authentication\n\nThis collection covers the 4 endpoints you'll use to build the login/signup flow for the frontend course: **Register**, **Login**, **Me**, and **Logout**.\n\n## How to use this collection\n1. Select the **Lecture 1 - Auth Environment** environment (top-right dropdown in Postman) so `{{baseUrl}}` and `{{token}}` are available.\n2. Make sure the backend is running locally (`npm run dev`) and you've seeded test data (`npm run seed`).\n3. Run **Login** (or **Register**) first. Its \"Tests\" tab contains a small script that automatically copies the JWT from the response into the `token` collection variable — you do NOT need to copy/paste it manually.\n4. Once `token` is set, **Me** and **Logout** will automatically send it as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.\n\n## Response shape\nEvery endpoint in this API replies with one of two shapes:\n\n```jsonc\n// success\n{ \"success\": true, \"data\": { ... } }\n\n// error\n{ \"success\": false, \"message\": \"Human readable message\", \"errors\": [] }\n```\n\n`errors` is populated (an array of `{ field, message }`) when the failure came from input validation; otherwise it's an empty array.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Lecture 1 - Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sarah Connor\",\n  \"email\": \"sarah.connor@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a brand new account.\n\n**What to send:** `name`, `email`, and `password` (min 6 characters) as JSON in the body.\n\n**What you get back:** the created user (never the password) plus a JWT `token` you can use immediately to call protected routes — that's why this request's Tests tab also auto-saves the token, just like Login.\n\n**Good to know:**\n- Every account created here always gets the `\"user\"` role, even if you try to send `\"role\": \"admin\"` in the body — the backend ignores that field on purpose. There is no self-service way to become an admin.\n- `email` must be unique. Trying to register an email that already exists returns a `400` with a validation-style error (see the saved \"Duplicate Email\" example response).\n- This is a **public** route — no `Authorization` header needed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", jsonData.data.token);",
                  "    console.log(\"Token saved from Register:\", jsonData.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Success - Account created",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sarah Connor\",\n  \"email\": \"sarah.connor@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "register"]
                }
              },
              "status": "Created",
              "code": 201,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"user\": {\n      \"id\": \"64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d2\",\n      \"name\": \"Sarah Connor\",\n      \"email\": \"sarah.connor@example.com\",\n      \"role\": \"user\"\n    },\n    \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOiI2NGYxYTJiM2M0ZDVlNmY3YThiOWMwZDIiLCJyb2xlIjoidXNlciIsImlhdCI6MTcwNTMxMjIwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzA1OTE3MDAwfQ.dGhpc19pc19hX2Zha2Vfc2lnbmF0dXJlX2V4YW1wbGU\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Error - Duplicate email",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sarah Connor\",\n  \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "register"]
                }
              },
              "status": "Bad Request",
              "code": 400,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Validation failed\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    {\n      \"field\": \"email\",\n      \"message\": \"Email is already registered\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ]
