        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin123\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs an existing user in and returns a JWT.\n\n**What to send:** `email` and `password` as JSON in the body. The example uses the seeded admin account (`npm run seed`) — swap in any account you've registered.\n\n**What you get back:** the user's profile plus a `token`. This request's Tests tab automatically saves that token into the `{{token}}` collection variable, so every protected request after this one (Me, Logout) \"just works\" without you copy-pasting anything.\n\n**Good to know:**\n- If the email or password is wrong, you get a `401` with a deliberately generic message (`\"Invalid email or password\"`) — the API never tells you *which* one was wrong, so an attacker can't use this endpoint to check whether an email is registered.\n- This is a **public** route — no `Authorization` header needed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", jsonData.data.token);",
                  "    console.log(\"Token saved from Login:\", jsonData.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Success - Logged in",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Admin123\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "login"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"user\": {\n      \"id\": \"64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1\",\n      \"name\": \"Admin User\",\n      \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n      \"role\": \"admin\"\n    },\n    \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOiI2NGYxYTJiM2M0ZDVlNmY3YThiOWMwZDEiLCJyb2xlIjoiYWRtaW4iLCJpYXQiOjE3MDUzMTIyMDAsImV4cCI6MTcwNTkxNzAwMH0.dGhpc19pc19hX2Zha2Vfc2lnbmF0dXJlX2V4YW1wbGU\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Error - Wrong credentials",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"wrongPassword123\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "login"]
                }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Invalid email or password\",\n  \"errors\": []\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the profile of whichever user the current `{{token}}` belongs to. This is the request you'd call right after your React app loads, to check \"is there a logged-in user, and who are they?\"\n\n**What to send:** nothing in the body — just a valid `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header. This is filled in automatically from the `{{token}}` variable (see the Authorization tab), which gets set after you run Register or Login.\n\n**What you get back:** the user's `id`, `name`, `email`, `role`, and `createdAt`. The password is never included.\n\n**Good to know:**\n- This is a **protected** route. If you run this before ever logging in (so `{{token}}` is empty) or after the token has expired, you'll get a `401`.\n- This is the perfect endpoint to poll on app startup to decide whether to show the login page or the logged-in app."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Success - Current user",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "me"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"user\": {\n      \"id\": \"64f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1\",\n      \"name\": \"Admin User\",\n      \"email\": \"admin@test.com\",\n      \"role\": \"admin\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z\"\n    }\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Error - Missing/invalid token",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "me"]
                }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Not authorized, no token provided\",\n  \"errors\": []\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Logs the current user out.\n\n**What to send:** nothing — just a valid `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header (auto-filled from `{{token}}`).\n\n**Important tradeoff to understand:** this API uses JWTs, which are stateless — the server never keeps a list of \"logged in\" tokens, so it has no way to invalidate one early. This endpoint just confirms the request was authenticated and returns a success message; the *actual* logout happens on the frontend by deleting the stored token (e.g. clearing it from `localStorage`/cookies). The old token would technically still be accepted by the API if someone replayed it, right up until it naturally expires (`JWT_EXPIRE`). That's a normal, accepted tradeoff for simple JWT auth — just make sure your React app always deletes its copy of the token here.\n\n**Good to know:**\n- This is a **protected** route, so it behaves like Me: no/invalid token → `401`."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Success - Logged out",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
                ],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "logout"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"message\": \"Logged out successfully\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Error - Missing/invalid token",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
                  "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
                  "path": ["auth", "logout"]
                }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Not authorized, no token provided\",\n  \"errors\": []\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
